{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-29T07:06:09.014Z","author":"codex-sol","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"0d410e0c5f36426d8cf3a920","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-7km8"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Upstream template SDK silently drops own __proto__ option keys"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Observed with @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.10.25: a valid user template containing an own __proto__ string option survives in stored JSON, but loadCreateTemplateOptions and runTemplatesShow return success while omitting that option. An ordinary option and constructor option survive. The upstream template parser and flag extractor clone arbitrary keys onto ordinary objects through indexed assignment. This is outside the pm-presets implementation; PR #170 preserves its own JSON dictionaries and refuses unsupported public-document keys and partial native projections until the host supports them safely."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["host-sdk","own-keys","templates","upstream"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-29T07:06:09.014Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-29T07:06:09.014Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"codex-sol"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Add adversarial own-key properties for SDK template parse/save/show and real CLI JSON/TOON, including Object.prototype names and prototype integrity on nongit trackers. Preserve expected SDK error identity. Revisit the pm-presets compatibility refusals after supported host versions preserve these keys."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Initialize a scratch tracker using PmClient with noExtensions. Write templates/own-key.json using JSON.parse for {\"name\":\"own-key\",\"options\":{\"__proto__\":\"public-data\",\"ordinary\":\"kept\",\"constructor\":\"kept\"}}. Call loadCreateTemplateOptions and runTemplatesShow through the pinned SDK. Both successful results omit __proto__ although the stored file retains the field. All data is synthetic."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Preserve every accepted option as an own data property, or return a typed refusal before accepting/writing unsupported input. Never change prototypes or silently produce partial data."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Both SDK reads omit __proto__; ordinary and constructor controls remain. SDK source confirms unsafe indexed assignment in template option cloning."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/affected_version","value":"2026.10.25"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"upstream template SDK"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"0aa9afde1c93f83e8c8742e613aebdc7259e676b100b0494abaf54ec5c67f299","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"1eec62758bbd09f104850d7ccf3bcbdc4c9a3838801fd58b8426fa7c370812bb"}
